---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro'
import AssertionCard from '../../components/AssertionCard.astro'
import ChartFigure from '../../components/ChartFigure.astro'
import Gloss from '../../components/Gloss.astro'
import { assertion } from '../../lib/feeds'
import { bar, line } from '../../lib/chart-spec'

const nineteen = assertion('nineteen-years-nineteen-losses')
const money = assertion('three-hundred-and-fifty-five-million-left')
const outearned = assertion('the-leavers-out-earned-the-arrivers')
const closing = assertion('the-income-gap-is-closing')
const south = assertion('more-than-half-who-leave-ohio-go-south')
const filedays = assertion('two-years-that-are-the-file')
const smaller = assertion('the-tax-file-finds-a-smaller-loss')
const foreign = assertion('foreign-migration-stops-being-published')

const named = assertion('forty-five-counties-and-six-hundred-and-ninety-seven-flows')
const churn = assertion('seventeen-thousand-crossings-of-one-county-line')
const border = assertion('the-border-comes-to-eighty-two')
const cities = assertion('the-loss-is-to-the-cities')
const columbus = assertion('columbus-is-a-fifth-of-everything')
const delaware = assertion('the-richest-leavers-go-to-delaware-county')
const fortwayne = assertion('two-allen-counties-and-the-ohio-one-loses')
const rural = assertion('five-rural-counties-give-more-than-they-take')
const missing = assertion('where-the-missing-people-went')

const yrs = ['2004–05', '2005–06', '2006–07', '2007–08', '2008–09', '2009–10', '2010–11', '2011–12', '2012–13', '2013–14', '2014–15', '2015–16', '2016–17', '2017–18', '2018–19', '2019–20', '2020–21', '2021–22', '2022–23']
const out = [3775, 3789, 3557, 3843, 3771, 3466, 3506, 3863, 3736, 3799, 2661, 3875, 5097, 3904, 3633, 4017, 3735, 3621, 3676]
const inn = [3206, 3043, 3048, 3303, 2999, 2768, 2918, 3226, 3616, 3225, 2483, 3261, 4385, 3365, 3328, 3633, 3540, 3335, 3471]
const outpe = [18626, 21244, 20297, 20311, 18909, 21278, 18072, 18425, 21539, 21156, 22601, 24079, 26924, 25652, 26014, 27937, 28359, 34206, 31862]
const inpe = [16469, 17184, 17885, 18784, 17275, 16853, 17393, 18760, 21650, 20003, 18509, 22883, 22296, 23182, 24271, 23371, 25921, 29373, 30149]

const netCats = ['Hardin', 'Putnam', 'Shelby', 'Mercer', 'Defiance', 'Van Wert', 'Auglaize', 'Lucas', 'Cuyahoga', 'Hancock', 'Montgomery', 'Wood', 'Butler', 'Allen, Ind.', 'Delaware', 'Hamilton', 'Franklin']
const netVals = [175, 145, 132, 101, 50, -12, -121, -161, -175, -269, -288, -308, -316, -326, -432, -443, -2036]

const classCats = ['Five counties on the border', 'Nine metropolitan counties', 'Thirty-one other named', 'Too small to name']
const classVals = [-82, -3981, -1266, -3842]

const flowSpec = line(
  yrs,
  [
    { name: 'left', y: out },
    { name: 'arrived', y: inn },
  ],
  { yTitle: 'Exemptions on tax returns that moved', labelLast: true, zeroBased: true },
)

const incomeSpec = line(
  yrs,
  [
    { name: 'those who left', y: outpe },
    { name: 'those who arrived', y: inpe },
  ],
  { yTitle: 'Adjusted gross income per exemption, dollars', labelLast: true, zeroBased: true },
)

const netSpec = bar(netCats, netVals, {
  yTitle: 'Net exemptions gained or lost, 2004–05 to 2022–23',
  labelValues: true,
})

const classSpec = bar(classCats, classVals, {
  yTitle: 'Net exemptions, nineteen years',
  labelValues: true,
})
---

<Article slug="where-they-went">
  <p>
    Every year the Internal Revenue Service matches the address on a tax return against the address
    on the same filer's return the year before, and publishes the result county by county with the
    money attached. Nineteen years of it exist. In all nineteen, more people left Allen County than
    arrived — 71,324 against 62,153 — and the largest single share of the difference went to one
    place.
  </p>

  <h2>Nineteen years of leaving</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={nineteen} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="flows"
    title="The two lines never cross"
    caption="Exemptions on tax returns moving into and out of Allen County. The dip in 2014–15 and the spike in 2016–17 are the file rather than the county: Auglaize and Hancock counties do the same thing in the same two years."
    columns={['Years', 'Left', 'Arrived', 'Net']}
    rows={yrs.filter((_, i) => i % 3 === 0 || i === yrs.length - 1).map((y) => {
      const i = yrs.indexOf(y)
      return [y, out[i], inn[i], inn[i] - out[i]]
    })}
    height={330}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="flows" set:html={JSON.stringify(flowSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={money} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={outearned} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="income"
    title="The people leaving have always earned more than the people arriving"
    caption="Adjusted gross income per exemption on the returns that moved. The two lines run apart for most of the record and have converged since 2018; both are nominal and neither is deflated."
    columns={['Years', 'Those who left', 'Those who arrived']}
    rows={yrs.filter((_, i) => i % 3 === 0 || i === yrs.length - 1).map((y) => {
      const i = yrs.indexOf(y)
      return [y, outpe[i], inpe[i]]
    })}
    height={320}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="income" set:html={JSON.stringify(incomeSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={closing} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={south} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={filedays} />
  <Gloss>
    Read alone, this county lost a third fewer people than usual in 2014–15 and half again as many
    as usual two years later, and a reader would want an explanation. Read beside Auglaize and
    Hancock, which move the same way in the same two years, there is nothing to explain: one year's
    matched returns arrived late and were counted in the next. Nothing in the file says so. The
    control had to come from the counties next door.
  </Gloss>
  <AssertionCard assertion={smaller} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={foreign} />

  <h2>Where they went</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={named} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={churn} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="net"
    title="Five counties give, and every city takes"
    caption="Net exemptions exchanged with each named county over nineteen years. The counties on the left are rural; the counties on the right hold or border a city of a hundred thousand people."
    columns={['County', 'Net exemptions']}
    rows={netCats.map((c, i) => [c, netVals[i]])}
    height={340}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="net" set:html={JSON.stringify(netSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={border} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={cities} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="classes"
    title="The border is even and the distance is not"
    caption="Allen County's net migration loss of 9,171 exemptions, split by where it went. Flows smaller than ten returns a year are suppressed into a regional residue, which is why 3,842 of the loss has a region and no county."
    columns={['Where', 'Net exemptions']}
    rows={classCats.map((c, i) => [c, classVals[i]])}
    height={290}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="classes" set:html={JSON.stringify(classSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={columbus} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={delaware} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={fortwayne} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={rural} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={missing} />
</Article>
